seg-e7f016777e09 = SURVEY ERROR. The station forms its correction against the coordinate it BELIEVES. An error there rides on every correction it broadcasts and reaches the user as -delta . u_ref -- which contains no user geometry at all, so unlike the orbit term it neither vanishes at zero baseline nor grows with baseline, and it transfers about one-for-one into the user's position. Default { "0.30" } m is the crate's own lunar reference (scenario file comment, lines { "64" } to { "70" })

# text
seg-e0648d9b52b4 = CORRECTION AGEING. A correction computed at t and applied at t+tau is stale two ways. Orbit: the satellite has MOVED, so the frozen orbit-error vector now projects onto a rotated line of sight; the rotation comes from this crate's own propagator, so no orbit-error rate is assumed anywhere. Clock: the satellite clock has drifted by c*sigma_y(tau)*tau for the full-RAFS power law in crate::clock_specs, calibrated the (scenario file comment, lines { "73" } to { "79" })

